artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $V=\bigoplus_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}V_{(n)}$ be a simple vertex operator algebra such that:
(i) $V_{(0)}=\mathbb{C}\mathbf{1}$ and $V_{(n)}=0$ for $n<0$;
(ii) $V$ is $C_2$-cofinite, i.e. the subspace $C_2(V):=\mathrm{span}\{u_{-2}v : u,v\in V\}$ has finite codimension in $V$;
(iii) $V$ is isomorphic to its contragredient module $V'$;
(iv) every grading-restricted generalized $V$-module is completely reducible.

Let $G$ be a finite group of automorphisms of $V$. For each $g\in G$, let a $g$-twisted (generalized) $V$-module be a vector space with a twisted vertex operator action satisfying the standard $g$-equivariance and grading-restriction axioms, and let a twisted intertwining operator of type $\binom{W_3}{W_1\,W_2}$ (where $W_i$ is $g_i$-twisted, $g_3=g_1g_2$) be defined in the sense generalized to non-commuting automorphisms (i.e. a linear map $W_1\otimes W_2\to W_3\{x\}[\log x]$ satisfying the appropriate twisted Jacobi identity, lower-truncation, and $L(-1)$-derivative conditions).

Prove or disprove: the twisted intertwining operators among the $g$-twisted $V$-modules, as $g$ ranges over $G$, satisfy
(a) the associativity property (existence of products of intertwining operators with convergent expansions),
(b) the commutativity property (analogous skew/braiding identity), and
(c) the modular invariance property (the spaces of $q$-traces or pseudo-$q$-traces of products of twisted intertwining operators are invariant under $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$).
